  "summary_en": "European Commission proposal for the Euro 7 Regulation, replacing Regulations 715/2007 and 595/2009. It sets tighter tailpipe and non-exhaust emission limits, battery durability minimums, on-board monitoring, anti-tampering and cybersecurity requirements for cars, vans, lorries and buses. It is conventional vehicle type-approval, with no AI or autonomy provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Single Euro 7 regulation merges light- and heavy-duty emission type-approval",
   "Stricter limits for tailpipe, brake, tyre and evaporative emissions, with extended durability",
   "Mandatory on-board monitoring (OBM), OBFCM and battery state-of-health monitors",
   "Anti-tampering and cybersecurity requirements referencing UN Regulation 155",
   "Application from July 2025 for cars/vans and July 2027 for heavy vehicles"
  ],
